  "note": "A beginner voice week at 15 minutes a day: a warm-up, an ear game and one longer musical piece that ends in a tune or line the student makes up. Every tune comes back in a second key through a Key selector, Do Mi Sol moves through three keys, one warm-up climbs a tempo ladder of stages and one opens with breathwork. Every note asked for is low in the voice, and where the singer could wander up the staff (the first staff, a slide, a skip up to Sol, a made-up line) one underlined care line says not to reach for high notes.",
  "plan": {
    "title": "Week 1: Do Mi Sol, in tune, your way",
    "summary": "Sing in tune over a drone and skip through Do Mi Sol, one idea a day: each day a short warm-up, an ear game, and a longer musical piece that ends with a tune or line you make up.",
    "progress": "Pitch: finds the low Do over a drone in C, D and F and hears when it settles; slides and hums into Sol. Next: find Do without the hum first.\nBreath & range: paced breath 3 to 6 counts, holds the low Do in G and D on \"oo\". All notes stayed in the low part of the range, with a line not to reach for high notes. Next: hold Sol, breath 3 to 7.\nIntervals & leaps: tells steps from skips, 3rds from 5ths and 5ths from 6ths by ear, sings Do Mi Sol in A, C and D and Do Re Mi on the beat up to 92 bpm. Falling skips are less sure. Next: sing a 4th.\nMelodies: easy step and skip tunes, each in two keys (C, D, G, A, F), one medium tune in A and D, own lines over two and three chords. Next: medium tunes in two keys.",
    "days": [
      {
        "theme": "Home over a drone",
        "exercises": [
          {
            "title": "Find the smooth spot",
            "minutes": 3,
            "level": "beginner",
            "area": "voice",
            "tags": [
              "sing"
            ],
            "topic": "voice-pitch",
            "why": "In tune with the drone sounds smooth and off sounds like a wobble, so the drone lets you check yourself with no one listening.",
            "learnBefore": [
              "/course/3/home-note"
            ],
            "cells": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Press Start exercise below: the drone and the mic start together. Your pitch shows as a line on the staff, the five lines of music.\nSing the low {{1}} on \"oo\" and slide a little above and below it until the wobble stops. Hold the smooth spot for as long as feels easy.\n_Don't reach for high notes: the low {{1}} is the only note this drill needs._"
              },
              {
                "type": "tool",
                "tool": {
                  "type": "staff",
                  "scale": "major-ionian",
                  "key": "c",
                  "voice": "tenor",
                  "labels": "solfege",
                  "enable": [
                    "1"
                  ],
                  "others": "hidden",
                  "drone": true
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
